.TH SDL_HINT_FORCE_RAISEWINDOW 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_FORCE_RAISEWINDOW \- A variable controlling whether raising the window should be done more forcefully.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_FORCE_RAISEWINDOW \(dqSDL_FORCE_RAISEWINDOW\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Honor the OS policy for raising windows\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Force the window to be raised, overriding any OS policy\[char46]
.PP
At present, this is only an issue under MS Windows, which makes it nearly impossible to programmatically move a window to the foreground, for \(dqsecurity\(dq reasons\[char46] See http://stackoverflow\[char46]com/a/34414846 for a discussion\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

